+# Organization-wide CommitLore Query System
+
+Enable decision searches across 40+ repositories without a database, service, or central server.
+
+## Architecture
+
+**The Challenge:** Querying all org repos currently requires cloning each (~40s per repo) and rebuilding indices. With 40 repos, that's 26+ minutes per query.
+
+**The Solution:** Federated Static Index Publishing
+- Each repo exports its derived index to JSON
+- Published via GitHub Releases (zero cost, built into GitHub)
+- A client tool (CLI or browser) downloads indices in parallel and queries them locally
+- Respects all constraints: no database, no service, no running costs, works offline
+
+```
+Repo 1                    Repo 2                    Repo N
+   ↓                         ↓                         ↓
+[build index]           [build index]           [build index]
+   ↓                         ↓                         ↓
+[export to JSON]        [export to JSON]        [export to JSON]
+   ↓                         ↓                         ↓
+[publish to Release]    [publish to Release]    [publish to Release]
+   ↓                         ↓                         ↓
+         ↖                    ↓                    ↗
+            ← Aggregator Tool ←
+                      ↓
+              Client-side query
+```
+
+## Setup
+
+### 1. Enable Index Publishing in Each Repository
+
+Add this GitHub Actions workflow to your repository (`.github/workflows/publish-commitlore-index.yml`):
+
+```yaml
+name: Publish CommitLore Index
+
+on:
+  push:
+    branches: [main]
+  workflow_dispatch:
+
+jobs:
+  publish-index:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+        with:
+          fetch-depth: 0
+
+      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
+        with:
+          node-version: "18"
+
+      - run: npm ci
+      - run: npm run build:index
+        # Command should export index to ./commitlore-index.json
+
+      - name: Create Release
+        uses: actions/create-release@v1
+        env:
+          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
+        with:
+          tag_name: commitlore-index-${{ github.run_number }}
+          release_name: CommitLore Index
+          draft: false
+          prerelease: true
+
+      - uses: actions/upload-release-asset@v1
+        env:
+          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
+        with:
+          upload_url: ${{ steps.create_release.outputs.upload_url }}
+          asset_path: ./commitlore-index.json
+          asset_name: commitlore-index.json
+          asset_content_type: application/json
+```
+
+The workflow:
+- Runs on every push to main (or manually)
+- Builds the index (assumed to export as `commitlore-index.json`)
+- Creates a GitHub Release
+- Uploads the JSON index as a release asset
+
+**Note:** If a repo doesn't have this workflow, the tool falls back to cloning and building locally.
+
+### 2. Create Org Configuration
+
+Create a manifest of repositories to query (e.g., `.commitlore/org-config.json`):
+
+```json
+{
+  "repositories": [
+    "https://github.com/myorg/repo1",
+    "https://github.com/myorg/repo2",
+    "https://github.com/myorg/repo3"
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Option A: Browser-based Query
+
+1. Open `web/org-query.html` in a browser (no server needed)
+2. Paste your org config JSON
+3. Enter search terms (trailer keywords, record ID, or path)
+4. Click "Search Across Repos"
+5. View results aggregated from all repos
+
+**Advantages:**
+- Zero setup
+- Works offline if indices are cached
+- No command-line knowledge needed
+- Shareable: just send the URL
+
+### Option B: CLI Tool
+
+```bash
+npx org-query \
+  --config .commitlore/org-config.json \
+  --trailer authentication
+```
+
+Options:
+- `--config <path>` - Path to org config JSON (default: `.commitlore/org-config.json`)
+- `--trailer <keyword>` - Search in decision text
+- `--record-id <id>` - Search in record ID (e.g., `r-abc123`)
+- `--path <pattern>` - Search in file path
+
+**Examples:**
+
+```bash
+# Find all auth-related decisions
+org-query --trailer authentication
+
+# Find specific decision record
+org-query --record-id r-2d55a9
+
+# Find decisions in a specific module
+org-query --path src/core
+
+# Combine filters
+org-query --trailer "database" --path infrastructure
+```
+
+### Option C: Programmatic API
+
+```typescript
+import { fetchAllIndices, queryFederatedIndices } from "@org/commitlore-federation";
+
+const repos = [
+  "https://github.com/myorg/repo1",
+  "https://github.com/myorg/repo2"
+];
+
+// Fetch indices in parallel (default: 5 concurrent)
+const indices = await fetchAllIndices(repos, { parallelism: 10 });
+
+// Query across all
+const results = queryFederatedIndices(indices, {
+  searchTrailer: "authentication"
+});
+
+// Process results
+for (const result of results) {
+  console.log(`${result.repo}: ${result.recordId} - ${result.trailer}`);
+}
+```
+
+## How It Works
+
+### Index Export
+
+Each repo's derived SQLite index is exported to JSON:
+
+```json
+{
+  "version": "1.0.0",
+  "repoUrl": "https://github.com/myorg/repo1",
+  "exportedAt": "2024-07-26T18:30:00Z",
+  "records": [
+    {
+      "recordId": "r-abc123",
+      "sha": "d940f5c2d7da323986055449ec16ce2b9d387116",
+      "path": "src/core/index.ts",
+      "trailer": "authentication flow redesigned to use OAuth2"
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### Index Publishing
+
+The GitHub Actions workflow:
+1. Builds the index (derived from git history)
+2. Exports to JSON
+3. Creates a GitHub Release (immutable, versioned)
+4. Uploads JSON as release asset
+
+**Why GitHub Releases?**
+- Free (part of GitHub)
+- Immutable and versioned
+- Works with GitHub API
+- No extra infrastructure
+
+### Query Aggregation
+
+The aggregator tool:
+1. Fetches published indices from all repos (in parallel)
+2. Merges them in-memory
+3. Runs queries client-side
+4. Gracefully handles missing/unavailable indices
+
+**Fallback:** If a repo doesn't have a published index, the tool skips it (not an error). Users can still clone and query locally if needed.
+
+## Performance
+
+With 40 repos and published indices:
+- **First query:** ~5-10 seconds (fetch 40 JSON files in parallel)
+- **Cached queries:** <1 second (work entirely offline)
+- **Comparison:** ~26 minutes with cloning per repo
+
+## Limitations & Tradeoffs
+
+| Aspect | Tradeoff |
+|--------|----------|
+| **Latency** | Published indices take ~5-10s to download. First commit doesn't appear in org-wide queries until workflow runs. |
+| **Freshness** | Queries show results from last workflow run, not live head. Acceptable for decision records (rarely change retroactively). |
+| **Availability** | If GitHub is down, org-wide queries don't work. Local clones still do. |
+| **Privacy** | Indices are published to GitHub Releases (public). Use a private GitHub org for sensitive repos. |
+
+## Constraints Satisfied
+
+✅ **No database** - Indices are just JSON files  
+✅ **No lookup service** - Static files hosted by GitHub  
+✅ **No server** - Works entirely with HTTP/GitHub API  
+✅ **Zero running cost** - GitHub Actions and Releases are free  
+✅ **Full feature set from clone alone** - Each repo remains self-contained  
+✅ **Index is derived, never committed** - Published before commit  
+✅ **Fallback for missing index** - Gracefully skips unavailable repos  
+
+## Future Enhancements
+
+- **CDN caching** - Cache indices in edge locations for faster downloads
+- **Delta updates** - Only export/publish changes since last run
+- **Search-as-you-type** - Backend aggregator for interactive queries (requires hosted service, relaxes constraints)
+- **Time-based queries** - Find decisions made in date ranges
+- **Decision relationships** - Cross-link related decisions (e.g., "superseded by")
+- **Org dashboard** - Visualize decision patterns across teams
